		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Adding Joint Makes Collison Spongy (Sequential Impulses)]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=3093#p3093"><![CDATA[
Hi, <br><blockquote class="uncited"><div>1. for each joint do PreStep<br><br>2. for each contact do PreStep<br><br>3. for each joint and contact apply correction impulses (iterate 10 times)? </div></blockquote>This should work better than the first version since you correct joints and contacts in the same iteration. Both, joints and contacts, define a position constraint and they have to be solved at the same time. Otherwise the dependencies between both are not taken into consideration.<br><br>Jan<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=818">Jan Bender</a> — Fri Jan 05, 2007 12:52 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
